  <p>Two talks shaped the approach: <a href="https://youtu.be/-QFHIoCo-Ko">Matt Pocock, “Full Walkthrough: Workflow for AI Coding”</a>, on clarifying requirements, vertical slices and dependencies between tasks; and <a href="https://youtu.be/rnDm57Py54A">Eric Zakariasson, “Building your own software factory”</a>, on isolated environments, parallel agents and better verification evidence.</p>
  <p>Among skill collections we looked at <a href="https://github.com/cloudflare/security-audit-skill">Cloudflare's security audit skill</a>, <a href="https://github.com/trailofbits/skills">Trail of Bits' skills</a>, <a href="https://github.com/addyosmani/agent-skills">Addy Osmani's agent skills</a>, <a href="https://github.com/anthropics/skills">Anthropic's skills</a> and <a href="https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable">Impeccable</a>. None is bundled: a project selects the skills its work needs.</p>
